## M66 — Clean-Room Pairwise Interop Harness

<!-- milestone-status: M66 planned -->
- **Status:** Planned.
- **Problem statement:** real pairwise publication is fail-closed because two independent
  conformance reports do not prove one bound bidirectional run.
- **Scope:** define a joint-execution format that binds two exact builds, shared run identity,
  cross-consumed artifacts, directionality, digests, and required verification material.
- **Explicit non-goals:** no waiver based on human summaries or two unrelated reports and no
  counting repository examples as independent implementations.
- **Principal evidence gap:** no joint pairwise execution artifact or validator.
- **Dependencies:** M62 and M64.
- **Completion criterion:** two clean-room test implementations can complete one bound run,
  the validator proves required cross-consumption, and incomplete/one-sided evidence fails
  closed.

## M67 — Security Coverage Closure

<!-- milestone-status: M67 planned -->
- **Status:** Planned.
- **Problem statement:** the repository has internal self-review and automated negative tests,
  but coverage remains partial for resync amplification/existence leakage and evidence
  privacy, and no independent external review artifact exists.
- **Scope:** close or explicitly defer threat-map gaps, add missing deterministic tests where
  protocol-observable, cover negotiation rollback/profile-composition downgrade and
  contract-substitution risks after their owning milestones, and prepare an external review.
- **Explicit non-goals:** no claim that platform rate limits or key custody are protocol
  guarantees and no fabricated external review.
- **Principal evidence gap:** partial threat rows and absent independent external report.
- **Dependencies:** M58; M60/M61 for their new threat surfaces.
- **Completion criterion:** every threat-map row has an accurate covered/partial/deferred
  status with linked tests or rationale, open remediations are tracked, and any external
  review claim points to an actual report.

## M68 — Governance and Standard Maturity

<!-- milestone-status: M68 planned -->
- **Status:** Planned.
- **Problem statement:** the current maintainer/steward model supports repository decisions
  but does not define the roles, voting, appeals, review cadence, or external-body structure
  expected of a mature open standard.
- **Scope:** document the real contributor/maintainer model, change-control process,
  succession, conflict handling, and a standards-maturity path.
- **Explicit non-goals:** no invented organization, maintainer, voter, committee, or external
  affiliation.
- **Principal evidence gap:** no complete standards-governance process beyond repository
  stewardship and PR/release decisions.
- **Dependencies:** M58.
- **Completion criterion:** governance documents define verifiable current roles/processes
  and clearly separate present authority from any future standards body.

## M69 — Release Engineering and RC Repackaging

<!-- milestone-status: M69 planned -->
- **Status:** Planned.
- **Problem statement:** version metadata is consistent at `0.1.0-rc.1`, but post-RC work is
  unreleased; snapshot naming remains `0.1.0-dev`; profile report outputs are inconsistently
  tracked; and local dependency/shell bootstrap is not cross-platform.
- **Scope:** decide generated-report policy, make local/CI dependency setup reproducible,
  align snapshot/release identifiers, package post-RC changes, and run the full release gate.
- **Explicit non-goals:** no version bump or final RC publication before the release decision
  and no fail-open release gates.
- **Principal evidence gap:** no coherent new-RC artifact set and no cross-platform clean
  checkout proof.
- **Dependencies:** M58, M67, and M68.
- **Completion criterion:** a clean checkout can reproduce all release artifacts/gates on
  supported environments, generated-file policy is enforced, and a maintainer-approved RC
  version is consistently packaged.

## M70 — External Plugfest Readiness

<!-- milestone-status: M70 planned -->
- **Status:** Planned.
- **Problem statement:** the public interop corpus contains no genuine independent external
  submission and pairwise evidence is unavailable.
- **Scope:** publish participant instructions, frozen TCK/release artifacts, intake/review
  operations, evidence/privacy rules, and a plugfest execution plan after prerequisite
  harnesses are ready.
- **Explicit non-goals:** no fictional participants, fabricated submissions, certification,
  or claim that readiness itself proves adoption.
- **Principal evidence gap:** zero real external submissions and zero pairwise-demonstrated
  runs.
- **Dependencies:** M63, M64, M66, M67, M68, and M69.
- **Completion criterion:** independent implementers can obtain the frozen artifacts, run the
  supported targets, submit eligible evidence, and participate in the pairwise process
  without repository-owned examples being counted as external proof.
